      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لَهُ إِنَّ رَجُلاً مِنْ مَوَالِيكَ مَاتَ وَ تَرَكَ وُلْداً صِغَاراً وَ تَرَكَ شَيْئاً وَ عَلَيْهِ دَيْنٌ وَ لَيْسَ يَعْلَمُ بِهِ اَلْغُرَمَاءُ فَإِنْ قُضِيَ لِغُرَمَائِهِ بَقِيَ وُلْدُهُ لَيْسَ لَهُمْ شَيْءٌ فَقَالَ \"أَنْفِقْهُ عَلَى وُلْدِهِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5564 - Muhammad ibn Ya'qub Al-Kulayni, may Allah (swt) be pleased with him, narrated from Humayd ibn Ziyad from Ibn Sama'ah from Sulayman ibn Dawud from Ali ibn Abi Hamzah from Abu Al-Hasan (as), peace be upon him, who said:\nI said to Imam (as): \"One of your followers passed away, leaving behind young children and some wealth, but he also had a debt that his creditors are unaware of. If the debt is paid, nothing will remain for his children.\"\nImam (as) said: \"Spend it on his children.\""
        ]
      }
    },
